    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: HID: wacom: fix out-of-bounds read in wacom_intuos_bt_irq (CVE-2026-43051)\n\n* kernel: ipvs: reload ip header after head reallocation (CVE-2026-68476)\n\n* kernel: ipvs: clear IPv4 options after rebasing tunnel ICMP errors (CVE-2026-74669)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: usx2y: bound the hwdep mmap fault offset (CVE-2026-74641)\n\n* kernel: Linux kernel IPVS: Denial of Service due to stale memory references (CVE-2026-80714)\n\n* kernel: ZDI-CAN-33367: Linux Kernel skbuff skb_zerocopy Improper Ownership Management Local Privilege Escalation Vulnerability ()\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
